# Release trust anchors of production office servers (legatto_env: prod).
# Installed to /etc/legatto/update/allowed_signers by the `updater` role,
# only inside a break-glass window; a release can never change this file.
# Adding a key later costs a break-glass window in every office, so all four
# keys below are added before the first office (RUNBOOK §0.2, §0.6).
#
# Format (ssh-keygen(1) ALLOWED SIGNERS), one key per line, no trailing comment;
# the "# <name>:" line above each key names it:
#   # release-a: YubiKey YK-2 (releases only)
#   release-a@legatto.pl namespaces="legatto-release,legatto-promote,legatto-index,legatto-revoke" sk-ssh-ed25519@openssh.com AAAA...
#   # release-b: YubiKey YK-3 (offline backup)
#   release-b@legatto.pl namespaces="legatto-release,legatto-promote,legatto-index,legatto-revoke" sk-ssh-ed25519@openssh.com AAAA...
#   # canary: generated on the canary server
#   canary@legatto.pl namespaces="legatto-canary" ssh-ed25519 AAAA...
#   # canary-b: offline backup attestation key
#   canary@legatto.pl namespaces="legatto-canary" ssh-ed25519 AAAA...
#
# release-a: FIDO2 key on the release YubiKey (YK-2), resident, verify-required,
#   application ssh:legatto-release; signs releases, promotions, the index and
#   KRLs. YK-2 holds nothing else (no SSH login, no age identity).
# release-b: the same kind of key on the offline YubiKey (YK-3), kept apart
#   from YK-2 with its PIN stored separately; used when YK-2 is lost or
#   broken. With signatures_required 1 either release key is enough.
# canary: software ed25519 key of the permanent canary server (P14), created
#   by the `updater` role, which prints this line ("Show the allowed_signers
#   line of this canary server"). Signs only attestations (legatto-canary);
#   it can never install or promote a release by itself.
# canary-b: software ed25519 key generated offline on day 0, private half kept
#   only age-encrypted to the YK-1 and YK-3 identities. Installed on a
#   replacement canary server before its `updater` role runs, so a new canary
#   needs no window in the offices. Same principal as `canary`: the updater
#   signs and verifies attestations as canary@legatto.pl; the key is the only
#   difference.
#
# Public halves: `ssh-keygen -K` with the YubiKey attached writes the resident
# key handles (id_ed25519_sk_rk_legatto-release*.pub); the software keys come
# with their .pub. Never invent or copy a key from elsewhere: each line is
# added by a reviewed, signed commit in legatto-node and pinned in legatto-infra.
#
# The role refuses legatto_env=prod until this file lists at least
# signatures_required release principals, all of type sk-ssh-ed25519.
# Software keys for tests live only in legatto-offices inventories with
# legatto_env: test (legatto_update_allowed_signers_src).
